      "finding": "plist",
      "explanation": "Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.",
      "remediation": "Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.",
      "code_snippet": "2. Therefore, what matters? Two metrics: click-through rate (getting people to click) and average/relative retention (watching longer than other videos)\n3. Strategy: If people click your video more than others AND watch it longer than others, that's what YouTube wants, and that's how you succeed\n\nKey insight: 'As simplistic as that is, that's what YouTube wants, and I think that's how you be successful.'\n\n### Netflix Flywheel (Simple Version) (Flywheels, flywheels, flywheels)\nA simplified Netflix flywheel that's more useful than the overly complex version",
